Let's assume the method is part of a class called `GroceryCostCalculator`. The method might look something like this:

```csharp
public class GroceryCostCalculator
{
    public double CalculateAverageMonthlyCost(decimal[] yearlyGroceryCosts)
    {
        if (yearlyGroceryCosts == null || yearlyGroceryCosts.Length == 0)
            throw new ArgumentException("Yearly grocery costs cannot be null or empty.");

        decimal totalCost = 0;
        foreach (var cost in yearlyGroceryCosts)
        {
            totalCost += cost;
        }

        return totalCost / yearlyGroceryCosts.Length;
    }
}
```

